==========================================================================
B. CUMULANT FORM OF THE CURVATURE
==========================================================================
  3x^2-2z-1  in cumulants  = -(2*kappa1*kappa3 - 3*kappa2**2)/kappa1**4
  target (3k2^2-2k1k3)/k1^4 = -(2*kappa1*kappa3 - 3*kappa2**2)/kappa1**4
  VERDICT B: IDENTITY HOLDS
  => curvature > 0  <=>  3 kappa_2^2 > 2 kappa_1 kappa_3.
     equal roots (kappa_2=kappa_3=0) is the exact zero of the curvature;
     symmetric root measures (kappa_3=0) give curvature 3 kappa_2^2/kappa_1^4 >= 0.

==========================================================================
C. MECHANISM: WHERE EACH OF 3x^2, -2z, -1 COMES FROM
==========================================================================
  log (d)_k = k log d - C(k,2)/d - S_2(k)/(2 d^2) - ... ,  S_2(k)=sum_{i<k} i^2
    Delta^3 [ -C(k,2) ] = 0  (quadratic -> 0)
    Delta^3 S_2(k) = 2  => +Delta^3 log(d)_k contributes -1 * d^-2   <-- THE '-1'

  k! e_k = d^k [ 1 - C(k,2) m2/d + (3C(k,4) m2^2 + 2C(k,3) m3)/d^2 + O(d^-3) ]
    (partitions of [k]: singletons -> d^k; one doubleton -> -C(k,2) m2 d^{k-1};
     two doubletons -> +3C(k,4) m2^2 d^{k-2}; one tripleton -> +2C(k,3) m3 d^{k-2})
    log-correction merges 3C(k,4) with -C(k,2)^2/2 :
      3C(k,4) - C(k,2)^2/2 = -(binomial(k, 2)**2 - 6*binomial(k, 4))/2 = k(k-1)(3-2k)/4  (CUBIC)
    Delta^3 of that cubic = -3  => -(-3) m2^2 = +3 m2^2
    Delta^3 [ 2C(k,3) ] = 2  => -(2) m3 = -2 m3
  => leading coefficient  3 m2^2 - 2 m3 - 1  (m1 = 1),  k CANCELS EXACTLY.
  VERDICT C: MECHANISM CONFIRMED

